{"nodes": [{"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1421", "label": "Register 1421 \u2014 the walk is a calendar, and the defect is the raggedness", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The calendar's raggedness is conventional \u2014 month lengths a political inheritance \u2014 while the walk's is a limit. Remove the limit and E goes to zero; remove February's oddity and you have a different calendar, not a complete one."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1422", "label": "Register 1422 \u2014 E is the count of missing elements, exactly", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shortening the last Janet block by k gives E = k one for one, so the index is complete the moment the table is. That makes it a prediction rather than a description: synthesise 119 and E drops to one, 120 and to zero. The control reproduced the compendium's calendar figure to the digit."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1423", "label": "Register 1423 \u2014 the atomic index is one hundred and twenty elements, and Janet said so in 1929", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An index that recovers Janet's count from its own arithmetic, without being told, is reading the subject and not its author \u2014 the reproduction is a stronger outcome than a prediction would have been."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1424", "label": "Register 1424 \u2014 Janet's E equal to zero is vacuous", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(n+l, Z) is one cell per element, so no envelope can bind and it cannot refuse anything \u2014 the same fault as Lambda_ladder's four-cell zero. The zero must be labelled forced, not earned; the demonstration that E is coordinate-relative survives."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1425", "label": "Register 1425 \u2014 what the one hundred and twenty changes, and what it does not", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The standing purpose is understanding rather than novelty, and on that axis a reproduction checkable against a century of chemistry is worth more than a prediction."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1426", "label": "Register 1426 \u2014 register 1395's limit split is wrong", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The split is 38/20, not 47/11. The limit used was the ground table's edge (Z=108), not the subject's (Z=118). The physics stands unchanged; only the accounting was wrong."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1427", "label": "Register 1427 \u2014 Lambda_ladder closes, E = 0 at nine cells", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The circularity is resolved from outside rather than by the closure itself \u2014 Lambda_PCA excluded the core independently, on different coordinates, before this was computed. The physics agrees: a K-alpha line measures the gap, so the seat is where the transition spans, not where the hole sits."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1428", "label": "Register 1428 \u2014 B2a resolved: five shared cells are four findings and one separation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two pairs are one object and the index is right to merge them (A = Z + N; Z = Ne + c \u2212 1), which is charge as one symbol in three positions appearing one level up \u2014 a finding, not a coordinate failure."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1429", "label": "Register 1429 \u2014 term and j ladders are five tower stages apart", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tower stage separates that pair and only that pair but costs closure (E 0 to 1), so it is recorded as the discriminator rather than seated as an axis."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1430", "label": "Register 1430 \u2014 C3, the nuclear claim survives its own falsifier by one shell", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 82\u2013126 shell contains both orientations and is exactly where kappa and mu are quoted as a unit, so regional freedom does not rescue the ordering. Tested against the thing that would have refuted it, and stronger for it."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_calendar_reading", "label": "The calendar reading of the walk index", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registered first as an analogy (1421) and then checked into an identity (1422): same shape, opposite status \u2014 the calendar's seven are conventional and permanent, the walk's two are a limit and will fall."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_walk_index_block_position", "label": "The walk indexed on (Janet block, position within block)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_janet_120_bound", "label": "The Z = 120 bound from the n+l = 8 block", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_lambda_ladder", "label": "Lambda_ladder", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_lambda_xray", "label": "Lambda_xray", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_lambda_pca", "label": "Lambda_PCA", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_lambda_spectra", "label": "Lambda_spectra", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_limit_ownership_rule", "label": "When an index has a limit, check whose limit it is", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The general fault register 1426 names: my data's edge was read as the subject's. Always ask whether the limit belongs to the subject or to the collection."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_singleton_rule", "label": "The singleton rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two outputs in one cell mean the observer is still choosing, so shared cells block a closure claim until each is adjudicated."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_contingency_protocol", "label": "The contingency protocol", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It separates an earned zero from a forced one by asking what fraction of comparable arrangements on the same grid refuse \u2014 90% for Lambda_ladder's nine cells; a construction that cannot refuse anything is vacuous."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_nilsson_six_pair_screen", "label": "The six-pair Nilsson screen", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1421", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_calendar_reading", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1421", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_walk_index_block_position", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1422", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1421", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/bridge/RAW-1421-1430.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_register_1422", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_bridge_raw_1421_1430_janet_120_bound", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confid